SUMMARY:Discussion & Reading of 2001: A Space Odyssey
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi all\,\n\nWe've been invited to an eve
 ning at the Symphony Space Leonard Nimoy Thalia Theater\, and I hope you c
 an make it! A panel of actors\, thinkers\, and writers will discuss Arthur
  C. Clarke's 1968 classic *2001: A Space Odyssey*. The panel will discuss 
 emergent artificial intelligence\, space exploration\, and the limits of h
 uman power. There will also be a reading from the prolific actor Stephen L
 ang (Avatar).\n.\n**Purchase your tickets for this event via the [Symphony
  Space website](https://www.symphonyspace.org/events/thalia-book-club-arth
 ur-c-clarkes-2001-a-space-odyssey)\, your rsvp to this Meetup event is not
  enough.** Use the code *Hal* at checkout to get your ticket at the specia
 l discount price of $15. Get your tickets asap\, this event will sell out!
 \n.\nOur Book Club read *[2001: A Space Odyssey](https://www.meetup.com/th
 escifibookclub/events/296342688/)* in 2024 and loved it. If you have not h
 ad the pleasure\, I highly recommend picking it up. The novel was written 
 by Clarke concurrently with Stanley Kubrick's writing of the film. It weav
 es in and out of what you've seen on screen\, crafted by one of the great 
 literary minds of our time. We'll likely discuss 2001 more at our [Open Si
 gnal virtual event](https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/3164389
 57) on November 12th.\n\nThanks again to Symphony Space for inviting us to
  this really interesting event!\n\nJon & Meghan
